    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "As one of the most prominent universal languages, music attempts to move its audience with emotions and ideas embedded within a few simple notes. This podcast addresses how external factors may influence our internal emotions and thoughts to give way to different music performances and listening experiences. In understanding social influences on mental composure within the realm of music, we may better comprehend and value the process in which we express ourselves to the world around us. \n\nThis podcast serves as the first episode within the \"Moving\" theme for the 2014 Sounds of Stanford PWR2 class taught by Christopher Gerben alongside podcasts by Tres Pittman and Jesse Leimgruber.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
